✅ Q20 — Find the First Non-Repeated Character in a String

🎗️ 20.1 Problem Statement

👉 You are given a String containing uppercase/lowercase letters and possibly repeated characters.
👉 Using Java Streams, find the first character that appears only once in the String.

Your solution should:

👉 Use the Stream API.
🔴 Return the result as an Optional<Character> or an appropriate nullable result.
🔴 Preserve the original character encounter order.
🔴 Correctly handle repeated characters.
🔴 Correctly handle uppercase and lowercase characters as distinct characters.
🔴 Correctly handle an empty String.
🔴 Do not use traditional for/while loops.

🎗️ 20.2 Input / Output

👉 Input

Use this exact String:
String input = "swiss";

👉 Expected Output w

Because:

s → appears 3 times
w → appears 1 time ✅
i → appears 1 time
s → appears 3 times
s → appears 3 times

The first character appearing only once is: w

Another Example

String input = "aabbcdd";
Expected: c

🎗️ 20.3 Your Task

Write the Java Stream solution.

You can provide:
🔴 Your primary approach
🔴 Any alternative approaches — Streams only
🔴 How you preserve encounter order
🔴 How you handle an empty String
🔴 How you handle a String where every character is repeated
🔴 Time and space complexity, if you want to attempt those too.



